  "scope": "Unchanged NodeList, NodeListIterator, Repository, DisconnectionQueue, TaskExecutor, TickUtils and LogoutListener on JDK 11, each case in a fresh class loader. Original text inserted at generation time: Player clear, finishClear, sendLogoutEvents, allowRemoval, getDetails, getName, getSession, setPlaying, isPlaying, getPacketDispatch, isArtificial, getCommunication and eight field declarations; PacketDispatch.sendLogout; IoSession disconnect, getPlayer, isActive, setObject and three field declarations; Node getName, getIndex, setIndex, isRenderable, setRenderable; NPC getId and its field; the Log and QueueStrength constants; the three ServerConstants values. Recording adapters: every other Player, Entity, PlayerDetails and IoSession member, combat, skills, death, teleport and script queue state, the logout packet, familiar, interfaces, Entity.clear, zones, house, UpdateSequence.renderablePlayers, the two management messages (with the generated builders' refusal of null strings), Player.checkForWealthUpdate, the clan, PlayerDetails.save, PlayerParser.saveImmediately, the log, sendMessage, the region chunk and Location equality, the selection key and socket. kotlinx.coroutines is a stand-in that keeps a launched block until the case runs it on the calling thread. The tick counter and its driver (update, then increment) are case inputs. The map cases drive java.util.HashMap itself. Not exercised: AIPlayer.clear, a null queue entry, concurrent callers, the save itself, real sockets, packets and coroutine dispatch.",
